{"name":"Blinking Terminal","hex":"#66cc00","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blinking","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That blinks.","bloody"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of blink"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blinking"},{"term":"terminal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building in an airport where passengers transfer from ground transportation to the facilities that allow them to board airplanes.","A harbour facility where ferries embark and disembark passengers and load and unload vehicles."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fatal; resulting in death.","Appearing at the end; top or apex of a physical object."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terminal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blinking","blocks":[{"text":"Blinking is a bodily function; it is a semi-autonomic rapid closing of the eyelid. A single blink consists of the closing of the eyelid or inactivation of the levator palpebrae superioris and the activation of the palpebral portion of the orbicularis oculi. It is an essential function of the eye that helps spread tears across and remove irritants from the surface of the cornea and conjunctiva."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blinking","wikidata":"Q1044679"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Eye_opening_and_closing.gif/250px-Eye_opening_and_closing.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/13/Eye_opening_and_closing.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Eye_opening_and_closing.gif/250px-Eye_opening_and_closing.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human eye blinking","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEye_opening_and_closing.gif"},{"